- name: stream_display_sink_0
  id: epy_block
  parameters:
    _source_code: "\"\"\"\nUses the 'sync' tag from the access-code correlator to know exactly where the\nheader starts, then uses openwave_link.FrameParser to collect exactly\nHeader+Payload+CRC32 bytes (per the header's real Payload Length field) and\nverify the CRC before publishing. No zero-run-terminator guessing - the header\ntells us exactly how many bytes to expect, and the CRC tells us whether we got\nthem right.\n\nTracks Sequence Number (gap/duplicate detection) and parses Flags from each\nCRC-verified frame - never from a CRC-failed one, since a corrupted header can\nstill unpack without a struct error while holding garbage values. Counts and\nthe last frame's seq/flags/mode/src/dst are published on the 'stats' port.\n\nstation_id (blank by default) is this receiver's own callsign. Blank means\n\"not configured to filter\" - every CRC-verified frame is accepted, which is\nalso the only sane default today since no TX chain populates a real\nDestination ID yet (openwave_link.py's docstring) - they all send the same\nall-zero placeholder. Once set, only frames addressed to station_id or a\nbroadcast (the literal 'ALL' callsign, or that same all-zero placeholder) are\nprocessed further; everything else is counted under 'not_for_us' and dropped\nbefore ACK/fragment/message handling - see openwave_link.is_for_station().\n\ncapture_file (blank by default = disabled) appends every completed frame\nattempt - 'ok', 'crc_fail', AND 'bad_length' alike, not just successful ones,\nsince a rejected frame is usually the more interesting one when debugging a\nreal problem later - to a file in exactly openwave_link.build_frame()'s byte\nformat (PREAMBLE + SYNC_WORD + whatever header/payload/CRC bytes were\nactually collected for that attempt). That means openwave_cli.py's `dump`/\n`recv` commands can process a capture file with zero changes - see\nopenwave_link.iter_frames()/describe_frames(). Opened in append mode so\nrestarting this flowgraph doesn't clobber a previous session's capture.\n\nDistinguishes three kinds of CRC-verified, for-us frame:\n  - ACK frames (openwave_link.is_ack): publish the acknowledged seq on\n    'ack_received' instead of trying to decode the (empty) payload as text.\n  - Fragmented Data frames: fed through openwave_link.FragmentReassembler;\n    'msg' is only published once the full run completes, transparently to\n    whoever's listening on 'msg' (a reassembled message looks identical to a\n    single-frame one).\n  - Plain Data frames: decoded and published on 'msg' directly, as before.\nA Data frame (fragmented or not) with the ack_requested flag publishes its\nseq on 'ack_needed'.\n\nNothing in this flowgraph currently transmits a real ACK back in response to\n'ack_needed', or feeds a real received ACK into 'ack_received' - RTL-SDR has\nno transmit capability at all, so this station can never send an ACK back\nover the air. These ports exist so the logic is ready for a future\nfull-duplex pairing.\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nfrom gnuradio import gr\nimport pmt\nimport sys, os\nif os.getcwd() not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, os.getcwd())\nimport openwave_link as link\n\n\nclass blk(gr.sync_block):\n    \"\"\"Sync-word-aligned, header-framed bit stream to message\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, tagname='sync', station_id='', capture_file=''):\n        gr.sync_block.__init__(self, name='Framed Stream to Message', in_sig=[np.uint8], out_sig=[])\n        self.tagname = tagname\n        self.station_id = station_id\n        self.capture_file = capture_file\n        self._capture_fh = open(capture_file, 'ab') if capture_file else None\n        self.parser = link.FrameParser()\n        self.reassembler = link.FragmentReassembler()\n        self.armed = False\n        self.bitpos = 0\n        self.curbyte = 0\n        self.counts = {'ok': 0, 'crc_fail': 0, 'bad_length': 0, 'dup': 0, 'lost': 0,\n                        'acks_rx': 0, 'frag_aborted': 0, 'frag_overflow': 0, 'not_for_us': 0}\n        self.last_seq = None\n        self.last_flags = 0\n        self.last_mode = 0\n        self.last_src = ''\n        self.last_dst = ''\n        self.message_port_register_out(pmt.intern('msg'))\n        self.message_port_register_out(pmt.intern('stats'))\n        self.message_port_register_out(pmt.intern('ack_needed'))\n        self.message_port_register_out(pmt.intern('ack_received'))\n\n    def stop(self):\n        if self._capture_fh is not None:\n            self._capture_fh.close()\n            self._capture_fh = None\n        return True\n\n    def _capture_attempt(self):\n        if self._capture_fh is not None:\n            self._capture_fh.write(link.PREAMBLE + link.SYNC_WORD + bytes(self.parser.buf))\n            self._capture_fh.flush()\n\n    def _publish_stats(self):\n        c = self.counts\n        seq_str = str(self.last_seq) if self.last_seq is not None else '-'\n        text = (f\"OK:{c['ok']}  CRC fail:{c['crc_fail']}  Bad length:{c['bad_length']}  \"\n                f\"Dup:{c['dup']}  Lost:{c['lost']}  ACKs rx:{c['acks_rx']}  \"\n                f\"Frag abort:{c['frag_aborted']}  Frag overflow:{c['frag_overflow']}  \"\n                f\"Not for us:{c['not_for_us']}  |  \"\n                f\"Seq:{seq_str}  Flags:{link.format_flags(self.last_flags)}  \"\n                f\"{link.format_mode(self.last_mode)}  \"\n                f\"Src:{self.last_src or '-'}  Dst:{self.last_dst or '-'}\")\n        self.message_port_pub(pmt.intern('stats'), pmt.string_to_symbol(text))\n\n    def _update_seq(self, header):\n        seq = header['seq']\n        if self.last_seq is not None:\n            if seq == self.last_seq:\n                self.counts['dup'] += 1\n            else:\n                gap = (seq - self.last_seq - 1) % link.SEQ_MODULUS\n                # Bound the gap we'll believe as real loss vs. e.g. TX having\n                # restarted (seq reset to 0) - avoids one bogus huge count.\n                if 0 < gap < 1000:\n                    self.counts['lost'] += gap\n        self.last_seq = seq\n        self.last_flags = header['flags']\n\n    def _update_addressing(self, header):\n        self.last_mode = header['mode_id']\n        self.last_src = link.decode_station_id(header['src_id'])\n        self.last_dst = link.decode_station_id(header['dst_id'])\n\n    def _publish_text_and_maybe_ack(self, header, payload_bytes):\n        self.counts['ok'] += 1\n        text = payload_bytes.decode('utf-8', errors='replace')\n        if text:\n            self.message_port_pub(pmt.intern('msg'), pmt.string_to_symbol(text))\n        if link.needs_ack(header):\n            self.message_port_pub(pmt.intern('ack_needed'), pmt.from_long(header['seq']))\n\n    def work(self, input_items, output_items):\n        in0 = input_items[0]\n        tags = self.get_tags_in_window(0, 0, len(in0), pmt.intern(self.tagname))\n        tag_offsets = {t.offset - self.nitems_read(0) for t in tags}\n\n        for i, bit in enumerate(in0):\n            if i in tag_offsets:\n                self.parser.reset()\n                self.armed = True\n                self.bitpos = 0\n                self.curbyte = 0\n\n            if not self.armed:\n                continue\n\n            self.curbyte = (self.curbyte << 1) | int(bit)\n            self.bitpos += 1\n            if self.bitpos == 8:\n                status, payload = self.parser.feed(self.curbyte)\n                self.bitpos = 0\n                self.curbyte = 0\n                if status == 'ok':\n                    header = self.parser.last_header\n                    self._update_seq(header)\n                    self._update_addressing(header)\n                    self._capture_attempt()\n\n                    if not link.is_for_station(header['dst_id'], self.station_id):\n                        self.counts['not_for_us'] += 1\n                    elif link.is_ack(header):\n                        self.counts['acks_rx'] += 1\n                        self.message_port_pub(pmt.intern('ack_received'), pmt.from_long(header['seq']))\n                    elif link.parse_flags(header['flags'])['fragmented']:\n                        frag_status, reassembled = self.reassembler.feed(header, payload)\n                        self.counts['frag_aborted'] = self.reassembler.abort_count\n                        self.counts['frag_overflow'] = self.reassembler.overflow_count\n                        if frag_status == 'complete':\n                            self._publish_text_and_maybe_ack(header, reassembled)\n                    else:\n                        self._publish_text_and_maybe_ack(header, payload)\n\n                    self._publish_stats()\n                    self.armed = False\n                elif status in ('crc_fail', 'bad_length'):\n                    self.counts[status] += 1\n                    self._capture_attempt()\n                    self._publish_stats()\n                    self.armed = False\n\n        return len(in0)\n"
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    comment: ''
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
    tagname: '''sync'''
    station_id: station_id
    capture_file: capture_file
  states:
    _io_cache: ('Framed Stream to Message', 'blk', [('tagname', "'sync'"), ('station_id', "''"), ('capture_file', "''")], [('0', 'byte', 1)], [('msg', 'message', 1), ('stats', 'message', 1), ('ack_needed', 'message', 1), ('ack_received', 'message', 1)], 'Sync-word-aligned, header-framed bit stream to message', ['tagname', 'station_id', 'capture_file'])
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate:
    - 976
    - 576.0
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
